**Read:** [Industrial Chemical Technology I — Adebayo, NOUN](../sources/Industrial-Chemical-Technology-I-NOUN.lingua#r_2026VMVXVJQGK3WTH1P17FE8T9), the complete introductory definitions and operation classifications; [Industrial Chemical Technology II — Nduka, NOUN](../sources/Industrial-Chemical-Technology-II-NOUN.lingua#r_7RXE2GF1DW7QH9GHTCGT0P09SR), the feedstock, product and flowsheet units; [Chemical Technology I — Indra Deo Mall, NPTEL](../sources/Chemical-Technology-I-Mall.lingua#r_2QDGEANAX8QTGRS531GFVF4H74), the introductory process-technology material and one full process description.

Separate a chemical species, a material stream and a commercial product. A stream may contain several species and phases; a product grade carries additional specifications. Feedstock, intermediate, reagent, catalyst, solvent, utility, co-product and waste identify roles in a particular process, and one material can occupy different roles in connected plants.

A unit process emphasizes a chemical transformation, while a unit operation describes a physical task such as distillation, filtration or heat exchange. Real equipment couples both: reaction may change phase behavior, evaporation may remove a product, and a catalyst's pore structure may control the apparent rate. A process name does not replace the governing chemistry and transport.

Build Portuguese/English meanings in context: matéria-prima/feedstock, corrente/stream, teor or composição/composition, rendimento/yield, conversão/conversion, seletividade/selectivity, purga/purge, reciclo/recycle, operação unitária/unit operation and especificação/specification. Keep the actual equation and denominator beside a quantity rather than trusting a familiar translation.

**Work:** annotate a complete published process description and flowsheet. Identify every material role and every consequential transformation/separation. Resolve three ambiguous terms with units, material state, boundaries and evidence. Explain a case where translating a word literally would conceal a different industrial definition.

